  "description": "Real Madrid paid 38 million pounds for a 16-year-old. Then he had to wait until he turned 18.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Vinícius Júnior: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vin%C3%ADcius_J%C3%BAnior\n\nFrom Wikipedia (Vinícius Júnior): born 12 July 2000 in São Gonçalo; his career began in 2006 when his father took him to Flamengo's branch in São Gonçalo; he made his senior debut for Flamengo in 2017 at age 16; on 23 May 2017 Real Madrid signed a contract to acquire him, effective after his 18th birthday on 12 July 2018 (18 is the minimum age for an international transfer), in a £38 million deal, a national record for a player under 18; he scored the only goal of the 2022 Champions League final against Liverpool; he scored in the 2024 final and became the youngest player to score in two Champions League finals, beating Lionel Messi's record; he was named The Best FIFA Men's Player for 2024. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #vinicius #realmadrid #howtheymakemoney",
